 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection algorithm in MATLAB, you need to add the gaussian filtering step as the first process in your code. Here's how you can modify the given code to implement the Sobel edge detection with a Gaussian filter:

```MATLAB
% Read input image and convert it to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

% Define the size of the Gaussian filter kernel (e.g., 3x3)
gaussian_kernel_size = 3;

% Create a standard normal distribution for generating the Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [gaussian_kernel_size gaussian_kernel_size], 0.5);

% Apply the Gaussian filter to the grayscale image
filtered_image = imfilter(double(gray_image), gaussian_filter, 'same');

% Define Sobel operator in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator in x and y directions to the filtered image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display the original image and the edge image
subplot(1,2,1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1,2,2), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');
```

