    // Set the auth token when it's available
    restServiceWrapper.SetAuthToken("your-auth-token-here");

    // Send GET request
    var response = await restServiceWrapper.GetAsync("/endpoint");

    // Handle response here
}
```

This example creates a simple `RestServiceWrapper` class with methods for sending GET and POST requests. The `SetAuthToken` method sets the `Authorization` header with the provided token. The main method demonstrates how to initialize the wrapper and set the token before sending a request.

