First, let's create a custom context for managing the toast messages and their display state. Create a new file named `ToastContext.js`:

```javascript
import { createContext } from 'react';

export const ToastContext = createContext();

export const ToastProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [toasts, setToasts] = React.useState([]);

  const addToast = (message) => {
    setToasts((prevToasts) => [...prevToasts, message]);
  };

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ toasts, addToast }}>
      {children}
      {toasts.map((toast, index) => (
        <ToastKey key={index} toast={toast} />
      ))}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

Next, create a functional component called `ToastKey.js` to render each toast message:

```javascript
// ToastKey.js
import { useContext } from 'react';
import { ToastContext } from './ToastContext';

const ToastKey = ({ toast }) => {
  const { removeToast } = useContext(ToastContext);

  const handleClick = () => {
    removeToast(toast.index);
  };

  return (
    <div className="toast" onClick={handleClick}>
      {toast.message}
    </div>
  );
};

export default ToastKey;
```

Now, you need to wrap your application with the `ToastProvider`. Wrap all your components in the `App.js` file like this:

```javascript
// App.js
import React from 'react';
import { ToastProvider } from './ToastContext';
import YourComponent from './YourComponent'; // replace with your main component

function App() {
  return (
    <ToastProvider>
      <YourComponent />
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

